
The name of the check-N.c file is used as a pointer to the file
../../tests/N-*.asn1. That ASN.1 file is compiled together with check-N.c
in a temporary directory. The check-N.c file contains the test engine.

For manual execution of a specific test case:

	./check-assembly.sh check-<NN>.c

check-65.c covers nested explicit and implicit BER tags on REAL aliases and
SEQUENCE members. Its complete values decode as zero (T1) and -1, +1, and +4
(T). Binary REAL contents include a format octet, an exponent, and a mantissa;
the old C0 00 and 80 00 contents omitted the mantissa and are rejection cases.
The test also checks truncated inputs and malformed tags and wrapper lengths.
The fixture was corrected after the issue #585 decoder hardening exposed it.


check-601 exercises SET CBOR maps with required and optional members, duplicate
known and unknown keys, truncated input, malformed descriptors, and flat
extension-group leaves beside direct map members. Duplicate names fail closed.
The indirect-choice 601 test covers CBOR table-selected SET open values in both
map orders, unknown selectors, optional omission, malformed selected data, and
generated SET/SEQUENCE cross-decoding of the same CBOR map.

check-604 covers direct IOC-selected SET XER values. Decoding a present open
member requires every other SET sibling to have appeared, because selector
callbacks do not expose their dependencies. Encoding also rejects a present
open member unless its canonical order follows every sibling. An incomplete open element returns
RC_WMORE without consuming that element; callers retain those bytes for replay.
A selected named NULL uses a nested self-closing type element; a self-closing <value/> is
rejected. Open leaves inside SET extension groups are unsupported and rejected.

check-605 covers C SEQUENCE CBOR maps with OPTIONAL and opaque ANY values,
deferred IOC-selected OPEN TYPE decoding in either key order, duplicate known
and unknown keys, missing required members, every truncated prefix, and
preservation of a preallocated value after a later map error. It also checks
restoration of an omitted DEFAULT value, unknown-key skipping, malformed UTF-8
key rejection, and a small deterministic fuzz seed corpus. An open member
requires all its sibling members to be present before the generated selector is
called because the selector API does not reveal which siblings it reads. The
SEQUENCE CBOR path rejects extension groups and multiple direct open members.

check-606 covers the one-entry CBOR CHOICE map, exact selected-child consumption,
UTF-8 text-key validation, unknown and malformed keys, truncated input,
nested child failure, preallocated value preservation, malformed descriptors,
and arbitrary-input decode cleanup through its fuzz entry.

check-609 covers issue #595: two-level top-level aliases of UTCTime,
GeneralizedTime, and NumericString retain their PER constraints for APER and
UPER. It checks independent golden UPER vectors, compares APER alias encodings
with the built-in descriptors, rejects invalid NumericString values and
reserved alphabet codes, and includes a SIZE-constrained NumericString alias
to verify inherited alphabet mappings.
